# Config dumps must never be touched. .EZHex starts with an XML header, so git
# would otherwise be entitled to treat it as text and rewrite its line endings —
# which would corrupt the binary blob and break both the declared size and the
# XOR checksum.
*.EZHex   binary
*.bin     binary
*.EZUp    binary

# Nothing under samples/ gets line-ending normalisation either. header.xml is a
# byte-exact slice of the container and uses CRLF; rewriting it to LF changes its
# length, which is exactly what <BINARYDATASIZE> and the checksum are there to
# detect. It has to stay as it came off the remote.
samples/** -text

* text=auto eol=lf
